  "content": {
    "id": "p34-q18-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "18",
    "prompt": "Find the digits $a$, $b$, and $c$ if $\\overline{abc}_{3}=\\overline{cba}_{4}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$a=2$, $b=1$, $c=1$.\n\nExpand both numerals using their place values and restrict the digits to those allowed in base 3.",
      "worked": "All three digits occur in base 3, so $b\\in\\{0,1,2\\}$. Since both numerals have three digits, $a,c\\in\\{1,2\\}$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}9a+3b+c&=16c+4b+a\\\\8a&=b+15c.\\end{align*}$$\n\nIf $a=1$, the left side is $8$, while the right side is at least $15$, so $a=2$. Then $b+15c=16$. Since $c=2$ would give at least $30$, $c=1$ and $b=1$.\n\nCheck:\n$$\\begin{align*}211_{3}&=2\\times3^{2}+1\\times3+1=22,\\\\112_{4}&=1\\times4^{2}+1\\times4+2=22.\\end{align*}$$\n\nTherefore, $a=2$, $b=1$, $c=1$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 84
  },
